'' NEVER STORED (PLAN B3): a root that expands __TIME__ (a hit would print the first build's
'' clock) and a root with a warning (a hit would not report it again). Each misses on the
'' second build, says why under -v (TKO0169), and the warning is reported again; a clean
'' root beside them hits.
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TKO_MODCACHE=build/.ucn/cache
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' CLEAN: build/.ucn
'' COPY: tests/driver/src/unitcache => build/.ucn/src
'' STEP: build -target windows-x86_64 build/.ucn/src/a.tiko build/.ucn/src/b.tiko build/.ucn/src/clock.tiko build/.ucn/src/warn.tiko -o build/.ucn/app.exe
'' ARGS: build -target windows-x86_64 build/.ucn/src/a.tiko build/.ucn/src/b.tiko build/.ucn/src/clock.tiko build/.ucn/src/warn.tiko -o build/.ucn/app.exe -v
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: unit build/.ucn/src/a.tiko: hit
'' EXPECT-OUT: unit build/.ucn/src/clock.tiko: miss (new)
'' EXPECT-OUT: note TKO0169: 'build/.ucn/src/clock.tiko' is not cached: it expands __DATE__, __DATE_ISO__ or __TIME__
'' EXPECT-OUT: warning TKO0312
'' EXPECT-OUT: note TKO0169: 'build/.ucn/src/warn.tiko' is not cached: it has warnings
